WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.871
"Wow!" Cole exclaimed. "That's awesome, Nathan.

2
00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:21.749
The judges really like your painting!"

3
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.202
But Patrick was frowning at Owen.

4
00:00:24.203 --> 00:00:27.780
"Are you sure you heard the judges right?" he demanded.

5
00:00:27.781 --> 00:00:30.535
"Did they mention my painting?"

6
00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:33.837
Owen shrugged. "Not while I was listening."

7
00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:38.035
Maggie smirked. "Too bad, Patrick," she said.

8
00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:41.788
"Come on, guys. We'd better get back to the lemonade stand."

9
00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:44.863
Henry and Cole followed her.

10
00:00:44.864 --> 00:00:48.460
"Do you think Nathan might actually win?" Cole asked.

11
00:00:48.461 --> 00:00:53.236
Henry shrugged. "He might. His painting is really good."

12
00:00:53.237 --> 00:00:57.214
Near the lemonade stand the fiddler had finished his performance.

13
00:00:57.215 --> 00:01:01.915
Now several bongo drummers were setting up their equipment on the bandstand.

14
00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:05.522
"It looks like we don't have any customers," Cole said.

15
00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:07.895
"Want to check out the crafts fair?"

16
00:01:07.896 --> 00:01:09.845
"Sure," Henry said.

17
00:01:09.846 --> 00:01:14.479
"Okay," Maggie agreed. "But we shouldn't stay away for long.

18
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.055
We'll probably have more customers when the music starts up again."

19
00:01:19.056 --> 00:01:21.994
The crafts fair was crowded and colorful.

20
00:01:21.995 --> 00:01:27.180
There were lots of interesting handmade items for sale everywhere Henry looked.

21
00:01:27.181 --> 00:01:31.312
Some of the booths featured demonstrations or classes too.

22
00:01:31.313 --> 00:01:35.084
Henry stopped to watch a woman churning butter by hand.

23
00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:39.636
Meanwhile Maggie waved at someone in the basket-weaving booth across the way.

24
00:01:39.637 --> 00:01:43.047
"Look," Maggie said. "There's Hannah."

25
00:01:43.048 --> 00:01:49.581
A dark-haired girl was sitting on a stool, weaving grasses into the shape of a large, flat basket.

26
00:01:49.582 --> 00:01:52.890
She looked up when The Lemonade Detectives approached.

27
00:01:52.891 --> 00:01:56.738
"Oh hi," Hannah said, pushing her hair out of her eyes.

28
00:01:56.739 --> 00:01:59.058
"It's the lemonade gang."

29
00:01:59.059 --> 00:02:03.643
"Hi." Maggie smiled at Hannah, looking at the basket in Hannah's lap.

30
00:02:03.644 --> 00:02:07.143
"Your parents have a booth every year, don't they?"

31
00:02:07.144 --> 00:02:11.903
Hannah nodded. "They look forward to Belltown Arts Day all year.

32
00:02:11.904 --> 00:02:16.645
They love showing off their baskets and teaching people about weaving."

33
00:02:16.646 --> 00:02:19.017
She pointed into the booth.

34
00:02:19.018 --> 00:02:23.225
Her parents were helping a young boy weave a small, round basket.

35
00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:24.979
Henry stepped inside.

36
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.265
The booth was filled with baskets of every size, shape, and color.

37
00:02:29.266 --> 00:02:33.872
"Wow," Henry said. "These baskets are really cool."

38
00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:39.871
Cole grinned. "Look, this one has a picture of a cat woven into it," he said.

39
00:02:39.872 --> 00:02:43.600
"Just like Nathan's painting! Did you make it, Hannah?"

40
00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.536
She nodded. "I love cats."

41
00:02:46.537 --> 00:02:49.960
"You should enter it in the art show," said Maggie.

42
00:02:49.961 --> 00:02:52.541
Hannah frowned. "No way.

43
00:02:52.542 --> 00:02:57.949
Those snobby art people don't want anything from the crafts booths in their contest.

44
00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:04.323
That's why the organizers made sure the crafts show was stuck way over here at the opposite end of the park."

45
00:03:04.324 --> 00:03:08.559
Henry was surprised. Hannah sounded really annoyed.

46
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.404
"Not all artists are snobby," Maggie reminded Hannah.

47
00:03:12.405 --> 00:03:15.102
"Our friend Nathan is really nice.

48
00:03:15.103 --> 00:03:19.059
He's a painter who might win the Under Twelve category this year."

49
00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:24.518
Hannah shrugged. "Whatever," she muttered, staring at the basket in her lap.

50
00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:28.912
Cole was digging through a bin full of small, colorful baskets.

51
00:03:28.913 --> 00:03:33.604
"Hey, how much is this one?" he asked, holding up one of the baskets.

52
00:03:33.605 --> 00:03:36.574
"I just remembered my mom's birthday is next week.

53
00:03:36.575 --> 00:03:39.695
She loves handmade stuff like this."

54
00:03:39.696 --> 00:03:44.218
Hannah told him the price, and Cole dug some money out of his pocket.

55
00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:48.022
Meanwhile Maggie grabbed Henry's phone to check the time.

56
00:03:48.023 --> 00:03:53.546
"Come on, you guys," she said as Hannah slipped Cole's basket into a small shopping bag.

57
00:03:53.547 --> 00:03:56.443
"We should get back to the lemonade stand."

58
00:03:56.444 --> 00:04:00.137
"Okay," Henry said. "See you, Hannah."

59
00:04:00.138 --> 00:04:08.637
"Bye," Hannah said. "Maybe I'll come by for some lemonade later if I have time."

60
00:04:08.638 --> 00:04:14.620
Back at the lemonade stand, Henry and the others were busy for a while serving thirsty customers.

61
00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:19.020
They knew all the customers. But then a stranger appeared.

62
00:04:19.021 --> 00:04:24.196
She was a very tall, very thin woman dressed in a shiny green dress.

63
00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:29.802
Her bright red hair was piled high atop her head and held in place with sparkly barrettes.

64
00:04:29.803 --> 00:04:33.840
Enormous white-framed sunglasses covered half her face.

65
00:04:33.841 --> 00:04:39.536
"One lemonade, please," she said, setting a quarter on the table.

66
00:04:39.537 --> 00:04:44.919
"Coming right up." Henry picked up a pitcher. "And welcome to Belltown."

67
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.594
The woman peered at him over the top of her sunglasses.

68
00:04:48.595 --> 00:04:54.298
Her eyes were suspicious. "What do you mean by that?" she demanded.

69
00:04:54.299 --> 00:04:57.146
"How do you know I don't live here?"

70
00:04:57.147 --> 00:05:00.986
Henry traded a surprised look with Maggie and Cole.

71
00:05:00.987 --> 00:05:07.345
"It was a guess," Henry replied. "Because we know almost everybody in town."

72
00:05:07.346 --> 00:05:11.740
"Yeah," Cole added. "Belltown is not very big."

73
00:05:11.741 --> 00:05:16.251
"How did you hear about Belltown Arts Day?" Maggie asked the woman.

74
00:05:16.252 --> 00:05:19.096
"I didn't think it was very famous."

75
00:05:19.097 --> 00:05:24.919
"Famous? What would someone like you know about being famous?" the woman snapped.

76
00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:28.359
Suddenly she spun around and rushed away.

77
00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:32.595
Cole stared after her. "What a weirdo!"

78
00:05:32.596 --> 00:05:36.477
"Yeah." Maggie picked up the quarter the woman had left.

79
00:05:36.478 --> 00:05:38.988
"She didn't even wait for her lemonade."

80
00:05:38.989 --> 00:05:40.823
Henry didn't answer.

81
00:05:40.824 --> 00:05:45.242
He'd just noticed Nathan rushing toward them, looking very upset.

82
00:05:45.243 --> 00:05:48.288
Nathan skidded to a stop in front of the stand.

83
00:05:48.289 --> 00:05:55.702
"My painting," he cried. "It's gone!"
